//RS //! The canonical merge engine (U5 — unified-ecosystem §6).
//RS //!
//RS //! One referee reconciles the typed contributions every module makes, across
//RS //! all three tiers (`env` / `system` / `image`). The §6 table:
//RS //!
//RS //! | Field | Rule |
//RS //! |---|---|
//RS //! | `sources` | merge by key; duplicate names with **different** refs conflict |
//RS //! | `packages` | concatenate, de-duplicate, **preserve source identity** |
//RS //! | namespace entries | merge by key; package lists combine; facts per below |
//RS //! | fact settings | one value wins by the shared contribution law |
//RS //!
//RS //! This is the pure data-reconciliation core (std-only, I6). It operates on the
//RS //! typed contribution model the module parser/evaluator will populate (Chunk 3+)
//RS //! and is independent of how those contributions are read. Conflicts are typed
//RS //! `MergeError`s here; they become I4 diagnostics when wired into evaluation.
//RS 
//RS use std::collections::BTreeMap;
//RS 
//RS pub use jet_foundation::Policy::{
//RS     ContributionLayer, FactContribution, FactError, FactKey, FactValue, SourceScope,
//RS };
//RS 
